BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 234.00 Td (This project is a multi-rail power management block for an SoC and sensor cluster. It) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 220.00 Td (takes a 5 V input and creates 1.2 V, 1.8 V, and 3.3 V rails. The rails are sequenced so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 206.00 Td (the core rail turns on first, then I/O, then sensors. I simulated the startup sequence) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 192.00 Td (and a 3.3 V load transient in LTspice, captured an ERC-clean schematic in KiCad,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 178.00 Td (included input protection, enable delay networks, output capacitors, loads, and test) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 164.00 Td (points, and documented the design limitations. The next production step would be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 150.00 Td (replacing the learning-model regulator choices with current-rated regulators, assigning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 136.00 Td (final footprints, doing PCB layout, and validating sequencing, ripple, transient) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 122.00 Td (response, and temperature on the bench.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 91.00 Td (19. Final Conclusion) Tj ET
